Changes on version 1.3.0 (2026-08-07, current):
- NSMutableNumber is now a genuine NSNumber subclass (was NSObject with an isKindOfClass:
  override). Equality with plain NSNumber is now symmetric, NSSet/NSDictionary lookups work
  in both directions, CFNumberRef toll-free bridging works, and inherited NSNumber API such
  as decimalValue is available (it previously raised unrecognized selector).
- classForCoder/classForKeyedArchiver return [self class] instead of a hardcoded class.
  Keyed archives still round-trip as NSMutableNumber; subclasses now keep their identity.
  Archivable subclasses must declare both overrides themselves (NSKeyedUnarchiver rejects
  inherited coder-class methods on subclasses of plist types); see the header.
- Factory constructors (+numberWithInt: etc., +zero/+one/...) use [self alloc], and
  copyWithZone:/mutableCopyWithZone: use [self.class allocWithZone:], so subclasses
  receive instances of their own class.

Changes on version 1.2.5 (2026-06-15):
- x86_64 support tweak

Changes on version 1.2.4 (2026-06-14):
- uses double rather than float.
- Real Xcode project
- Real GitHub workflow
- rm 32 bit int paths for 64 bit systems

Changes on version 1.2.3:
- Changed NaN to notANumber, for alignment with NSDecimalNumber.
- copy the class numbers like zero, one, infinity, etc.
- Property to construct special number: one, for alignment with NSDecimalNumber.
- Corrected Construction Category

Changes on version 1.2.2:
- Better `compare:` method to replicate output of NSNumber, especially around NotANumber.
- NSCoder support for older non-keyed coding (for older versions of Apple OSes).
- Properties to construct special numbers: infinity, negative Infinity (minusInfinity), NaN, zero, and negative Zero (-0.0 double).
- Better isNegativeOne
- Adds isPositiveZero and isNegativeZero for real numbers.
- Greater unit test coverage
- NSMockNumber to test different data types that aren't used by NSNumber.

Changes on version 1.2.1:
- Adds bitNot to NSNumber and NSMutableNumber for returning the bitNot number.
- Adds bitNotValue (as an unsigned long long) to NSNumber and NSMutableNumber.
- Adds plusOne and subtractOne to return their respective classes NSNumber and NSMutableNumber adding and subtracting 1.
- Adds addOne and minusOne to NSMutableNumber for incrementing and decrementing.
- Adds isNegativeOne, isZero, isOne, isTwo, isThree, isFour, isFive, isNAN, isInfinity, and isNegativeInfinity properties to NSNumber and NSMutableNumber.
- Adds unichar type support to NSNumber and NSMutableNumber.  "unicharValue" is a new type that is returned; setable in NSMutableNumber. (Unichar is unsigned short).
- Enables support for NSSecureCoding.
- Updates Unit Tests for all the above added functionality.

Changes on version 1.1.4:
- Add NSMutableCopying protocol to NSNumber.
- Add NSMutableCopying protocol to NSMutableNumber

Changes on version 1.1.3:
- Tests small fix.

Changes on version 1.1.2:
- Split C++ and Objective-C implementation.

